WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.590
Roll two dice again and again,
adding the scores each time.

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.440
The totals run from two up to twelve.

3
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.700
Keep a tally.

4
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.060
As the rolls pile up, the
middle bars race ahead.

5
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.240
The ends barely move.

6
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.500
Which total wins in the long run?

7
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:21.030
And why should any total win,
when every face is equally likely?

8
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:26.070
In this mission, you'll list every
outcome of two dice in a six by six grid.

9
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.700
You'll see why a one then a
six, and a six then a one,

10
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.930
are two different outcomes.

11
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.900
And when outcomes are equally likely,
you'll find a probability by counting:

12
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.730
the outcomes you want, over the total.

13
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.040
Your mission: work out which
total is most likely, and why.
